# M100 Audio Works licensing

Copyright (c) 2026 Metzger100 and project contributors. Existing authorship and copyright notices remain applicable.

Owner decision: 2026-10-05. This policy covers all project-authored material in this repository, including every module, generated output and preserved project-authored snapshot. The licences apply by the purpose of the material as described below; they are not alternative licences from which a recipient may choose.

## Software and other project-authored material

**SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later**

Software, scripts, tests, build and simulation tooling, software schemas, repository policies, general research reports, indexes, project-authored artwork and other project-authored material outside the hardware-source scope are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or, at your option, any later version published by the Free Software Foundation. This includes copyrightable project-authored data compilations; the licence does not create copyright in facts.

You may redistribute and/or modify this material under those terms. It is distributed without any warranty, including the implied warranties of merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose. See the [complete GPL text](LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt).

## Hardware design sources

**SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0**

Project-authored hardware design sources are licensed under the CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2, Strongly Reciprocal. This covers circuit netlists and electrical design models (including project-authored SPICE `.cir`, `.spice`, `.sp` and `.subckt` files), candidate `topology.yaml` files, hardware proposal descriptions, design specifications, schematics, PCB/layout files, mechanical design files, BOMs and documentation needed to make or modify the hardware. Simulator programs that generate or evaluate these sources remain software under GPL-3.0-or-later. The same distinction applies to copies in experiment snapshots and generated design outputs.

You may redistribute and modify this Covered Source and make products using it under the terms of CERN-OHL-S-2.0. This Covered Source is distributed without any warranty, including the implied warranties of merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose. See the [complete CERN licence text](LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.txt).

Source Location: [the Audio Works repository](https://github.com/metzger100/audio-works). Design publication does not establish hardware qualification or third-party patent clearance; the [patent policy](PATENTS.md) and engineering evidence requirements remain applicable.

## Third-party material and historical notices

These grants cover only rights held by the project authors. Original third-party datasheets, photographs, measurements, quoted material, vendor models and derivatives, downloaded packages, fonts and licence texts retain their own copyrights, notices and terms. In particular, reference material in `meridian-microphone/research/reference-datasheets/`, acquired vendor/source evidence and embedded third-party portions of snapshots are excluded from the project grants. Project-authored acquisition metadata and commentary retain the applicable project licence. The [Source Serif font notice](branding/design/tools/SourceSerif-LICENSE.md) remains intact. Where redistribution permission is unresolved, no permission is supplied by this policy.

The former current MIT notice at `meridian-microphone/lab/LICENSE` has been removed. Previously distributed MIT copies retain their existing permissions; this decision does not revoke those grants or rewrite Git history. Frozen historical notices describe their original capture and are preserved as provenance. Current project-authored material is offered under the scope above, with required third-party notices preserved.

The complete licence texts are unmodified copies from the [SPDX GPL record](https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-3.0-or-later.html) and [SPDX CERN record](https://spdx.org/licenses/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.html), retrieved on 2026-10-05. Adding these licences does not publish private backups or authorize purchases, contacts, payments or release of an unqualified implementation.
